# The world where INV-03 has been adjudicated — an overlay for the derivation
# test, NOT part of the committed corpus. INV-03 (the cyber inspection floor
# against the control budget) resolves by au:Narrow; wo-042, whose ONE live
# hold reached it through the federal-reliability leg of its closure,
# releases to READY, and wo-046 — held three more ways — does not. That
# asymmetry is the test: resolving a conflict releases exactly the orders it
# alone was holding, which is spec#45's done-bar at the derivation layer.
@prefix au:  <https://aion.savvi.io/ontology/authoring#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix amp: <https://ampere.example/corpus#> .

amp:INV-03 au:resolvedBy amp:r-inv03-test .
amp:r-inv03-test a au:Resolution ;
    au:outcome au:Narrow ;
    au:decidedBy amp:p-import ;
    au:decidedAt "2026-08-20T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    au:rationale "Test overlay: inspection window narrowed to the maintenance interval, so the 180 ms floor and the 150 ms budget stop overlapping." .
